<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Dollar sign, not the riyal sign: Saudi Arabia's new official riyal glyph (Unicode U+20C1,
     added 2025) still has patchy font support on-device, and its calligraphic shape isn't
     something safe to hand-draw as vector paths without a visual preview. This is a blocky,
     geometric $ built the same way as the old bar-chart icon (straight rectangles, one existing
     arc technique) rather than smooth curves, for the same reason. Ask for a riyal-sign attempt
     if you'd rather see that instead once this is on the phone. -->
